  "lifecycle": {
    "tool": "bench_decision_context lifecycle",
    "per_cycle": "model create; chat opened (max 1 token); context at the largest geometry (T = 1024, capacity 1216) opened and warmed with one batch of all 16 questions; a second context on the same weights opened, used once and closed; 100 measured batches of one question each (q01..q16 in turn), each bit-identical to the warm batch; every 10th index first a chat turn, an invalid batch (duplicate question IDs, must be INVALID with zero answers) and a cancelled batch (must be CANCELLED with zero answers); at index 50 the context is closed and opened again (reset/recovery); context closed, chat closed, model destroyed",
    "cycles": 3,
    "requests": 100,
    "process": "the three cycles in one process; where three cycles exceed the section limit (Bonsai NEON) one process per cycle, and the cross-cycle growth check is then reported as not observable (never PASS)",
    "synchronization": "every sample follows a completed synchronous call (scoring includes device synchronization); nothing runs concurrently",
    "counters": "runtime decision-wrapper live allocations/bytes, process RSS (mach resident_size) and the backend's scoped MTLDevice.currentAllocatedSize, each reported on its own; none is total system GPU memory",
    "budgets_rule": "#17's rule plus room for two FP32 contexts at the largest geometry: max = 1.5 x file bytes + 2 GiB (RSS and Metal); after the model is destroyed 1 GiB RSS; Metal is readable only with a model loaded",
